# Versioning

MailGent is **0.1.x alpha** until v1. Follow global SemVer (`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`).

## Version bump = CHANGELOG entry (same commit)

**Never bump `MARKETING_VERSION` without updating root `CHANGELOG.md` in the same commit.**

1. Add a `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD` section at the top (below the title blurb).
2. Group bullets under `### Added`, `### Fixed`, `### Changed`, or `### Breaking`.
3. One section per release; do not edit past sections except typos.

Backfill missing history when you discover a gap (as with 0.1.0–0.1.3 before `CHANGELOG.md` existed).

## Files to keep in sync

| File | Field |
|------|-------|
| `project.yml` | `MARKETING_VERSION`, `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION` |
| `MailGent.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj` | regenerate via `xcodegen generate` after `project.yml` |
| `README.md` | `**X.Y.Z alpha**` headline |
| `PRIVACY.md` | `This X.Y.Z alpha binary…` |
| `MailStore/Sources/LoopbackMCPServer.swift` | MCP `initialize` → `serverInfo.version` |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | new top section for the bump |

Increment `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION` on every release build.

## Git

- Do not land versioned work on `main` — branch `feat/…` or `fix/…` first.
- Tag the release commit `vX.Y.Z` when shipping.
- Docs/chore/internal-only: no version bump, no CHANGELOG entry.
